<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Dronningruta low coastal leg: Stø–Nyksund — Stø–Nyksund low coastal leg [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Walk only the low coastal leg from Stø via Skipssanden and Langvaddalen to the pass between Mælen and Sløymarkheia, descend the west valley, then follow the approximately 1 km gravel road into Nyksund. The high mountain loop and its rope sections are excluded. Arrange return transport before setting out. The complete mapped course is about 7.015 km; the 7.0 km distance and 310 m ascent/descent are approximate planning figures. The 150-minute duration is a historical approximate estimate, not a current operator time. Climbing estimates come from a historical 10 m terrain model, not a field survey; allow tens of metres uncertainty. Prepare for wind, rain, slippery ground and changing coastal weather. Check current local conditions and obey closures; managed source records do not guarantee access today.

Route geometry: © Kartverket — https://www.kartverket.no/; Tur- og friluftsruter / Turrutebasen Fotrute, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Recorded maintainer: DNT Vesterålen. Changes: original EPSG:25833 source coordinates transformed to WGS84 and ordered into the original low coastal course; no invented joins or elevation assigned.

Terrain-derived approximate metric facts separately: © Kartverket — https://www.kartverket.no/; DTM10 UTM33 dataset dddbb667-1303-4ac5-8640-7ec04c0e3918 (https://www.geonorge.no/geonetwork/srv/api/records/dddbb667-1303-4ac5-8640-7ec04c0e3918/formatters/xml), CC BY 4.0. Historical model last updated 2013, 10 m resolution; bilinear interpolation on every original edge at intervals up to 10 m, centered 25 m mean with actual endpoint terrain heights, rounded to 10 m. Unsmooth/50 m/100 m sensitivity spans about 267–336 m; allow tens of metres uncertainty. Terrain supplies factual metrics only, not route geometry or public elevations. Descriptive planning geometry, not navigation-grade.

Route geometry: © Kartverket — https://www.kartverket.no/; TurOgFriluftsruter / Nasjonal database for turruter. Identify contributing maintainer, source, licence and coordinate transformation/retrace changes per route. — Kartverket Turrutebasen released TurOgFriluftsruter walking features. Licence: CC-BY-4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Source: https://www.geonorge.no/geonetwork/srv/api/records/d1422d17-6d95-4ef1-96ab-8af31744dd63/formatters/xml. Dataset: https://www.kartverket.no/geodataarbeid/det-offentlige-kartgrunnlaget-dok/turruter.</desc><trkseg><trkpt lat="69.01893552451034" lon="15.123436558345674"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01889983910002" lon="15.123176096593527"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01886142343328" lon="15.122845550161555"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01882774058004" lon="15.122542558816923"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01880105417862" lon="15.122237104790718"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01875996819003" lon="15.122001641610815"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01875550191467" lon="15.121976591858914"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01870437473337" lon="15.121736069085214"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01865969189315" lon="15.121513100439996"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01862148005164" lon="15.121270148535164"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.0185837900372" lon="15.121049722648417"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01854110579166" lon="15.120789230511473"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01850882250955" lon="15.120531298861382"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01847866659648" lon="15.12030841412632"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.0184491609798" lon="15.120053001543369"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01842244037881" lon="15.119790097440635"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01839047528256" lon="15.119459599170224"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01836540636333" lon="15.119141651484359"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01834237696312" lon="15.118856247398302"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01832185645274" lon="15.118573359886993"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01830412599173" lon="15.118275473238283"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.01828467725782" lon="15.117997597402892"></trkpt><trkpt lat="69.018